{"repositoryId":1408497266,"availability":"available","full":"JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop","name":"jpkcom-desktop","description":"Desktop-style web interface in plain JavaScript: windows, Dock and apps in the browser. No build step, no dependencies.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T08:40:45Z","updated":"2026-10-09T12:28:27Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.jpkc.com/desktop/","topics":["browser-desktop","desktop","development","webapp"],"demo":"https://jpkcom.github.io/jpkcom-desktop/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.188Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.188Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.188Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.188Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A desktop-style web interface in plain JavaScript: windows, a menu bar, a dock and apps, in the browser.","Live demo · Your own site in 10 minutes · Use this template (the button at the top of the repository page) to start your own copy.","JPKCom Desktop turns a website into a desktop built on the classic desktop metaphor. Pages open in windows that can be moved, snapped to an edge and restored on the next visit. A menu bar, a dock, desktop icons, an \"All apps\" grid and a quick search lead to the content. The project includes an editor, notes, tasks, a calculator, a terminal, media players and more. Everything is a set of static files: native ES modules, no build step, no runtime dependencies and a strict Content Security Policy. You can put it on any web server, at the root or in a sub-folder."],"features":["Move, resize, minimise and zoom windows; double-click or double-tap a title bar to zoom.","Drag a window to the left or right edge to fill that half of the screen, or to the top edge to zoom it.","A preview shows where it will go. Rest the pointer on the zoom button to open a tile menu (left half, right half, full size, both side by side).","Overview (F3 or Ctrl+↑) shows every window scaled side by side. Ctrl+\\ switches to the next window.","Session restore: open windows come back on the next visit. Visitors can switch this off."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"30a5f70517ec0c39ada35b1fa54ced191f563fb876c76bbd801469000667edd6","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.421Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.421Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A desktop-style web interface in plain JavaScript: windows, a menu bar, a dock and apps, in the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Modules: a calendar with ISO week numbers; public holidays that are computed, never fetched (the de-by region is included as an example); weather from Open-Meteo or Bright Sky (opt-in); notification banners from a JSON Feed per language; and the vault, encrypted private bookmarks that unlock with login in the terminal.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"They are encrypted into a file on the server, and login in the terminal decrypts them in the browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"30a5f70517ec0c39ada35b1fa54ced191f563fb876c76bbd801469000667edd6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.422Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T12:28:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/JPKCom/jpkcom-desktop/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T19:33:21.425Z","hash":"30a5f70517ec0c39ada35b1fa54ced191f563fb876c76bbd801469000667edd6","originalBytes":92602,"storedBytes":92602,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["self","site","header","desktop",